    "file_name": "XIN_ENG_20061130.0252.tml",
    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061130.0252\n\nBEIJING, Nov. 30 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nChina launches mid-term examination of rubber dumping measures\n\n\n\n\nChina's Ministry of Commerce issued a bulletin on Thursday to launch a mid-term examination of measures against dumping by a petro-chemical company in the Republic of Korea (ROK).\n\nThe examination into the alleged dumping of styrene butadiene rubber was scheduled to end within a year, according to the ministry.\n\nROK-based Kumbo Petrochemical Co., Ltd. submitted an application to the ministry in September for a mid-term examination, asking China to lower its 10 percent tariff rate.\n\nStyrene butadiene rubber is a chemical material used in the manufacture of tires and other rubber products. China levied an anti-dumping tax on imported rubber from Russia, the ROK and Japan in September 2003.",
